Z||000012||BN Boomer||10-23-2001||05:19 PM||||Why don't we get cars like that?<P>Because enough people keep voting Democrat/Green/Socialist etc. They want their government to be their nanny. In their continual efforts to save us from ourselves, they have legislated mandatory safety standards and imposed them on the rest of us. It's not enough for them to reduce their own exposure to risk, they must force their veiws on the rest of us. Seat belt laws, helmet laws, airbags that may even kill us, etc. After all, "It's for the children", right?<P>Contrary to a rather uninformed claim above, the current SUV fad is only the latest manifestation of the general public's desire not to be shoehorned into some sub-compact econobox or forced onto public transportation just because the Sierra Club, Earth First, Greenpeace, Al Gore, or Ralph Nader think we should, believing themselves to be some sort of omniscient power possesing an exclusive knowledge of what is best for the rest of us. Automotive manufacturers are simply doing what any decently managed company does in a capitalist economy, responding to the economic laws of supply and demand (which in this case have been articially altered/manipulated to a significant degree due to government interference). ||||reg||1
