Z||000017||AusFiero||10-23-2001||07:27 PM||||Probably time for me to jump in here. The HSV is definately not the same platform as any Cadillac or Opel. It was based loosely on an Opel before it was stretched, widened and strengthened to handle Australias shitty roads. The suspension and everything on the platform is purely Australian developed. Well except the 5.7 ltr Chev motor.<BR>The HSV comes in many different forms from a supercharged 3.8 litre up to the GTS with the 300kw and 5.7 6 speed gearbox. <BR>At HSV they start with Holden delivered cars then turn them into something a little special you might say. Yes HSV stands for Holden Special Vehicles.<BR>Most people over here are eagerly awaiting a HSV version of the new Monaro pictured below. We and our press have been lead to believe that it will be the replacement for the killed of F-Body but lo and behold it was on the news the other day that the Monaro badge is getting dropped for the HSV cars and they are to be called GTOs. Only sold here though, for now. When they do hit America eventually they will be probably still the f body replacement.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp_0247.jpg"> <P>And here is what they look like as everyday cars. Well not quite everyday as this is an ex cop car. This is my wifes Commodore. Well mine but you know women once they claim something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/commodore4_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
