Z||000023||bHooper||10-24-2001||09:03 AM||||Well, I got a reply back about the Kamala.  It's not exactly what I was looking for, but I will post it anyway.<P>"10th September 2001<P><BR>We are pleased to announce that as from 5th September 2001, Tony & Mark Keen will take over the Kamala Project. This will include, all sales ~ kits & complete cars, after sales & spares etc. Tony & Mark are very experienced in servicing & restoring high quality cars and we have every confidence that the Kamala is going to a good home! As a company DAX feel that they will be able to give the outstanding Kamala and its customers the time & attention it & they need to be able to fulfil its enormous potential.<P>As far as DAX is concerned this will not be a cut & run sale, as we will be working with Tony & Mark for a long period to ensure a smooth transition for them, our existing customers and their future customers.<P>Prices will remain the same for sometime and will be listed on our website for the near future.<P>The new contact address is:<P>Tony & Mark Keen<BR>Kamala Cars<BR>The Drift<BR>Chapel Bell<BR>Crownthorpe<BR>Wymondham<BR>Norfolk NR18 9EW<P>Tel. No: 01953 605911<BR>e-mail kamala@kamalacars.freeserve.co.uk"<P>i will email the new crowd with the same questions.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
